                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-7" aria-label="Return from footnote 7.">Return to 7</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-8">See Mark Bils and Peter J. Klenow, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="offsite" href="http://klenow.com/StickyPrices.pdf">&ldquo;Some Evidence on the Importance of Sticky Prices,&rdquo;</a> Journal of Political Economy 112, 2004, pp. 947-985, and Emi Nakamura and J&oacute;n Steinsson, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="offsite" href="http://www.columbia.edu/~en2198/papers/fivefacts.pdf">&ldquo;Five Facts about Prices: A Reevaluation of Menu Cost Models,&rdquo;</a> Quarterly Journal of Economics, November 2008, pp. 1415-1464.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-8" aria-label="Return from footnote 8.">Return to 8</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-9">Bharat Trehan and Maura Lynch, <a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="offsite" href="http://www.frbsf.org/economic-research/publications/economic-letter/2013/november/consumer-inflation-expectations-us-uk-japan-oil-prices/">&ldquo;Consumer Inflation Views in Three Countries,&rdquo;</a> Economic Letter, Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco, November 2013.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-9" aria-label="Return from footnote 9.">Return to 9</a>
                    </li>
        </ol>
</div>
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>
</div>    <div class="component notes">
        <div class="component-content">

				
					
					
					
					
					
					

					  
						
						  
							
						
					
					
					 
						
							
											
					
					
					
						
					
					
							
						
					
				     
			
